# Airtable Scraper Service

This project includes a background service that scrapes a public Airtable shared view on a configurable cron schedule and stores the results in a dedicated PostgreSQL table.

---

## File Map

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `backend/src/services/airtableScraper.js` | Core scraper: fetch HTML → extract params → call API → parse → upsert DB |
| `backend/src/routes/airtableDeals.js` | REST API for reading scraped deals + triggering manual scrapes |
| `backend/src/db/migrate.js` | Contains `create_airtable_deals_table` migration (already added) |
| `backend/src/index.js` | Imports scraper service (side-effect import) and mounts route |
| `backend/.env.example` | Documents the 3 scraper env vars |

---

## How the Scraper Works (4 Steps)

### Step 1 — Fetch the shared-view HTML
```
GET https://airtable.com/appEGxhjno0HTpEco/shrUhtbnzZTPaR4Lk/tblACIQ9QNiVmoWSK
```
- Uses a real browser `User-Agent` to avoid bot detection
- Collects all `Set-Cookie` headers (needed for Step 3 auth)

### Step 2 — Extract API parameters from embedded JS
Parses the HTML for three values:
- **`urlWithParams`** — internal API path containing the view ID + access-policy token
  Pattern: `urlWithParams:\s*["']([^"']*readSharedViewData[^"']*)["']`
  Unicode-escapes (`\u002F`) are decoded to `/`
- **`x-airtable-application-id`** — e.g. `appEGxhjno0HTpEco`
- **`x-airtable-page-load-id`** — e.g. `pglXXXXXXX`

### Step 3 — Call `readSharedViewData` internal API
```
GET https://airtable.com/v0.3/view/{viewId}/readSharedViewData?{accessPolicy}
```
Required headers: `Cookie`, `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest`, `x-airtable-application-id`, `x-airtable-page-load-id`, `x-airtable-inter-service-client: webClient`, `x-user-locale: en`, `x-time-zone: America/New_York`

Returns JSON with `data.table.columns` (column definitions + select choices) and `data.table.rows` (all rows in one response — no pagination).

### Step 4 — Parse and upsert
- Build a `columnId → { dbField, type, choices }` lookup from `COLUMN_MAP`
- For each row, resolve cell values (number, text, select, multiSelect, button, date)
- Bulk-upsert via `ON CONFLICT (airtable_id) DO UPDATE` — safe to re-run at any frequency

